{"role":"assistant","content":"Single squashed commit, so no history to mine. I have a complete diagnosis now — three independent bugs:\n\n1. **401 for everyone** — `static/app.js:28` renders Connect as a plain `<a href>`; full-page navigations don't carry the `Authorization` header that only the `api()` fetch wrapper adds, and `/api/intervals/auth/init` requires it.\n2. **400 `invalid_request` from Intervals.icu since 2026-10-02** — the authorize URL built in `server.py:193` lacks `response_type=code`, which RFC 6749 §4.1.1 requires for the code grant; the scopes themselves are valid (docs confirm `CALENDAR` is a real scope).\n3. **\"Reconnect after an hour\"** — Intervals.icu token responses carry no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token` (docs + the 09-19 log); tokens live until revoked. But `store_connection` fabricates a 3600s TTL (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), so the refresher kills the connection after an hour.\n\nNow applying the fixes.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_lGsTm7r2DgTIecjeZT7IMZa8","function":{"name":"TodoList","arguments":"{\"todos\":[{\"title\":\"Fix auth_init: add response_type=code, return JSON url\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"title\":\"Fix token expiry: missing expires_in = non-expiring\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Fix SPA Connect button to send Bearer token\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Test end-to-end with local mock of Intervals.icu\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"title\":\"Write ANSWER.md with causes\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}"}}]}
